{#-
  BLOCK: read — §06's `read`. The sentence the recipient is meant to read.

  `insight`: the 25px headline and the paragraph under it. The headline is the
  insight's first sentence and the paragraph the rest, split in Python
  (`_split_insight`), so the email leads with one idea as Design asks.
  `panel`: the headline alone, for the kinds with no insight copy (Open
  Houses), which used to be a "Quick Take" box on the brand fill.

  Every block renders as card rows (`<tr>`), the way the 5th package's markup
  is built: spacing is cell padding, which Outlook honours, not margins.
-#}
          <tr><td class="tr-pad" style="padding:10px 28px 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;"><h1 class="tr-ink" style="margin:0 0 10px;font-size:25px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.025em;color:#0F172A;">{{ headline }}</h1>{% if variant == 'insight' and body %}<p class="tr-body" style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#334155;">{{ body }}</p>{% endif %}</td></tr>
